<%# The two SHIPPED wallet modals, rendered through the engine's real modal host,
    so a real browser can drive their real catch blocks.

    BOTH partials by name. Nothing here restates what either does — the catch
    block, the mapper call, the `typeof` guard and the try/catch around the
    report are all the gem's, and they are the entire subject of the specs. A
    page that hand-rolled any of it would leave the specs grading the lab.

    WHAT THE SCRIPT BELOW SUPPLIES IS THE HOST'S HALF, and every line of it is a
    global this gem does NOT ship: window.walletProvider and
    window.solanaConnectAndVerify are turf-monster's wallet_provider.js,
    parseSolanaError and reportWalletFailure are its solana_errors.js. The gem's
    shipped JavaScript tree is the network guard plus the redirect-transport
    set (wallet_transport, redirect_provider, wallet_journal, wallet_ops) and
    none of them defines any of these globals. The lab is the host here, so the lab provides them — the same
    relationship /lab/modal has to Solana::Network.describe.

    STAND-INS SHAPED FROM THE SHIPPED ARTICLE, not from what makes a spec pass.
    parseSolanaError below carries ONE real rule copied verbatim out of
    turf-monster's mapper — the insufficient-funds pair — because a stub shaped
    to suit the test certifies the test. That pair is also the incident: a
    correct mapper meeting a wallet string it had never seen is how an empty
    Phantom was answered with balance advice seven times in one production
    session on 2026-09-06. %>
<main data-test="wallet-failure-lab">
  <%= render "studio/modals/host" do %>
    <template x-if="$store.modals.current().id === 'wallet-connect'">
      <%= render "solana_studio/modals/wallet_connect" %>
    </template>
    <template x-if="$store.modals.current().id === 'web3-step-up'">
      <%= render "solana_studio/modals/web3_step_up" %>
    </template>
  <% end %>
</main>

<script>
  // What the wallet will refuse with. A spec sets this, so the error the gem
  // catches is a real rejected promise from the real call site rather than
  // something the page handed the partial directly.
  window.labRejectWith = null;

  // Every report the gem made, in order. A spec asserts on LENGTH as well as
  // content: "reported once" and "reported twice" are different outcomes and the
  // upstream-dedupe guard is the difference between them.
  window.labReports = [];

  window.reportWalletFailure = function (stage, provider, raw, mapped) {
    window.labReports.push({
      stage: stage,
      provider: provider,
      raw: raw,
      mapped: mapped,
      // The gem must pass FOUR values and add nothing of its own. `opts`,
      // `verifyArgs()` and `this.props` are all in scope at the wallet-connect
      // call site and carry currentUserId; a fifth argument would mean one of
      // them leaked into an error log.
      arity: arguments.length
    });
  };

  // ONE rule, copied verbatim from turf-monster app/javascript/solana_errors.js.
  // Enough to make `raw` and `mapped` genuinely DIFFERENT strings, which is the
  // property the reporting exists to preserve.
  window.parseSolanaError = function (msg) {
    if (/insufficient funds/i.test(msg)) {
      return 'Insufficient USDC balance. Top up your wallet via the Faucet.';
    }
    return msg;
  };

  window.walletProvider = {
    available: function () { return [{ name: 'Phantom' }]; },
    get: function (name) { return name === 'Phantom' ? { name: 'Phantom' } : null; },
    isMobile: function () { return false; }
  };

  // Rejects, always — this lab exists for the failure path. A REAL rejected
  // promise from the real await, so the gem's own catch block is what runs.
  window.solanaConnectAndVerify = function () {
    return Promise.reject(window.labRejectWith || new Error('lab: no rejection configured'));
  };

  window.labOpenPicker = function () {
    window.Alpine.store('modals').open('wallet-connect', {});
  };

  window.labOpenStepUp = function () {
    window.Alpine.store('modals').open('web3-step-up', {
      provider: 'Phantom',
      providerLabel: 'Phantom',
      walletHint: 'ABCD…4321'
    });
  };
</script>
